  DepthGainMin: 0.35
  DepthGainMax: 1.3
  Why: The kit profile's strongest harmonic is a 4.00 m rib that comes round exactly with the 12 m tile, so a long run read as one scallop at one pitch (St Peters east bank, 11-20). The shift slides where each rib falls along the shore (two scales, three angles each, wavelengths off every fraction of 12 m); the depth gain makes neighbouring ribs stand proud or nearly flush. Both are functions of the plan position only, so chunk cuts stay closed.
